      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure. Please see the modules that are touched by the submitted-together changes. `apexd.microdroid` is a good example. Both `apexd` and `apexd.microdroid` are installed to `/system/bin/apex`. https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/q/topic:%22hide_from_make%22\n\nre: make `installable: false` act the same as `no_full_install: true`\n\nThe problem of `installable` is that it\u0027s not available to every module (i.e. `android.Module`). I could go in that direction, but that would be been a much more intrusive change; I didn\u0027t like that. Another reason was that the expression `installable: false` is misleading because we still do install the module to filesystem modules.\n\nI think, in the long term, we should deprecate `no_full_install` (while keeping `installable`) if we stop making filesystem image in Make.",
